artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $\mu_0$ and $\mu_1$ be two positive Borel measures on the real line with finite moments. Consider the Sobolev inner product
$$\langle f,g\rangle_S \;=\; \int f(x)\,g(x)\,d\mu_0(x) \;+\; \int f'(x)\,g'(x)\,d\mu_1(x),$$
and let $\{Q_n\}_{n\ge 0}$ denote the sequence of monic polynomials orthogonal with respect to $\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_S$.

The asymptotic behavior of $Q_n$ (outer relative asymptotics with respect to the standard orthogonal polynomials for $\mu_0$, Mehler–Heine type asymptotics, and asymptotic zero distribution) is known in the case where $\operatorname{supp}(\mu_1)\subseteq\operatorname{supp}(\mu_0)$ is a compact set, by means of algebraic identities available for the (discrete or continuous) Sobolev product in that nested situation.

Determine the asymptotic behavior of $\{Q_n\}$ in the following non-nested configurations, where those algebraic identities are not available:
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] $\operatorname{supp}(\mu_0)\cap\operatorname{supp}(\mu_1)=\emptyset$ (disjoint supports);
\item[(b)] $\operatorname{supp}(\mu_0)\cap\operatorname{supp}(\mu_1)\neq\emptyset$, but neither support contains the other (overlapping but non-nested supports).
\end{enumerate}
In each case, establish (i) the outer relative asymptotics of $Q_n(z)$ off the supports, (ii) Mehler–Heine type local asymptotics, and (iii) the limiting distribution of the zeros of $Q_n$.
